# Data-provenance investigation notes (2026-08-07) -- working analyses of the
# MODIS/VIIRS phase-function source files, shared between the author and the
# phase-function programmer. Kept in the working folder for easy access by both,
# but deliberately NOT published to the public repo: they discuss unresolved
# discrepancies in third-party source data, not VISTA-C behaviour.
NOTE_pf_norm_forward_peak_resolution.md
g_comparison_old_vs_new.md

# MODIS phase functions in netCDF4 (source data; converted browser assets, when
# they exist, will live elsewhere and be tracked separately)
MODIS_Phase Functions_netCDF4/

# C5 high-N chunk intermediates (tests/DISORT comparisons/modis-viirs/).
# 5 x 20 M jump() sub-streams per band, 40+ files, ~1.4 MB, fully regenerable from
# vistac_run_chunk.mjs. Never tracked historically -- the committed artifacts are the
# summed results (C5_results_*_100M.json) and the figures. Keeping the raw chunks out
# avoids ~1.4 MB of regenerable binary-ish JSON per high-N campaign.
tests/DISORT comparisons/modis-viirs/vista_*_c[0-9]*.json
